;;; A hypothesis `(not ?g)` with `?g` bound to a guest put `(not Ann)` in H —
;;; regression `not-name-hrule-concluded`.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, of whom Ann has paid, and a hypothesis rule that supposes `(not ?g)` of
;;; whoever has paid.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `(not Ann)` is the negation of no fact, so it is no hypothesis: refused, one line,
;;; on every command. Without the rule's candidate H is empty and R is {∅}. Under
;;; `open`, `(not ?g)` is no fact's spelling, and the parse refuses it.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `55aadd0b`, release: the program loaded; H was the one candidate `(not Ann)`, and R
;;; two states, ∅ and {(not Ann)}, which differ in a fact nothing can read: the goal
;;; answered `?g = Ann` in both, exit 0 on every command.
;;; The engine refuses it at the parse.
;;;

(relation paid Guest :why "{?3} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(paid Ann)
(rule suppose () :match (paid ?g) :assert (open (not ?g)) :why "suppose not {?g}")
(query :goal (paid ?g))
